// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
// Filename:	 Flood Array PCB.test
// Project:		VSC80,90,900
// Author:      Foster & Freeman Ltd - Paul Evans
// Modified:    28/05/24
//
// Description: Tests the  Flood Array PCB LED's
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.

#1: Enter operator initials and PCB serial number:
a. Enter operator intials.
b. Enter serial number into the box below.
IMPORTANT: Observe ESD precautions for handling ESD sensitive devices.  
DISPLAY: 260-022.png
CLICK_OK:

#2: Equipment Setup 1
a. Using TE159 connect the PSU to the VSC90 Controller Test Box(TE209).
b. Connect the PC (via USB) to K5 on the Test box (TE209).
c. Connect the PC (via USB) to the TENMA Programmable PSU.
d. Connect the PC to the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
DISPLAY: FloodSetup.png
CLICK_OK:


#3: Equipment Setup 2
a. Connect the UUT to the VSC90 Controller Test Box(TE209).
b. Place the UUT inside the LED Test Box with Web Camera (TE086).
c. Set the TENMA Programmable PSU power switch to on.
CLICK_OK:
EXE: OpenWinCam.bat
CONNECT: TENMAPSU
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #3: 

#4: Configure the PSU
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCP1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCPSET1:500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:12.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:1.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET2:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET2:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1

#4.1: Power on the test box.
Press the I/O Power button on the VSC90 Controller Test Box(TE209) to turn on.
DELAY: 7000
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.086 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
IF:
GOTO: #4.2: 
IMPORTANT: This test has failed, check the power button has been pressed, power supply, USB connection and the ftdi chip.		
PASS_FAIL: #4.1
GOTO: #5

#4.2: Connect to the test box
CONNECT: VSC90


#5: Test box f/W  version check
COMMAND: VSC90  BUILD
READLINE: VSC90  BUILD
IF:
Check the Test box is programmed correctly.
COMMAND: VSC90  TYPE
READLINE: VSC90  TYPE
Returned product is = %TYPE%
Returned Version is = %BUILD%
ELSE:
Bad result . . . No communication to PIC device
PASS_FAIL: #5


#6: Voltage check
COMMAND: VSC90 READVOLTS 
READLINE: VSC90 READVOLTS 
Returned Voltage is = %READVOLTS%
RANGE: %READVOLTS% 12000 50					
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#7: Tests the I2C to the EEPROM and 3.3V supply
COMMAND: VSC90  ENUM
READLINE: VSC90  ENUM
Check the expected result is a match.
Expected result is = LFLOOD,ZOOM,EEPROM,
Returned result is = %ENUM%
[%ENUM% STR_EQ LFLOOD,ZOOM,EEPROM,]// evaluates inside the [] and set true or false flag
SUB: TestPassOrFail // sends the outcome to flag to the subroutine for evaluation


#8: Check white LED's 3 & 4
COMMAND: VSC90 W12 1023
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.261 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail
// CLICK_OK:

#9: Check white LED 9
COMMAND: VSC90 OVD 2 1023
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.190 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#10: Check white LED 10
COMMAND: VSC90 OVD 4 750
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.161 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#11: Check UV LED's 7, 8, 13
COMMAND: VSC90 UV365 1023
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.428 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail
// CLICK_OK:

#12: Check  IR780 LED's 6 & 5
COMMAND: VSC90 IR780 1023
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.210 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail
// CLICK_OK:

#13: Check  IR850 LED's D1 & D2
COMMAND: VSC90 IR850 750
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.216 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail
// CLICK_OK:

#14: Check  IR940 LED's D3 & D4
COMMAND: VSC90 IR940 1023
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.249 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail
// CLICK_OK:

#15: Check  IR980 LED's 1 & 2
COMMAND: VSC90 IR980 1000
DELAY: 1500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned current is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.184 0.010 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail
// CLICK_OK:

#16: Test complete
COMMAND: VSC90 If#	// turn off any LEDs still on: 
#17: Test complete
IF: %FAILED% > 0
GOTO: #Failed:
ELSE: #Passed:

#Failed: a test failed
This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
Check the Log file for more details on the failed test(s).
IMPORTANT: This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
DISPLAY: test_failed.png
CLICK_OK:
GOTO: #QUIT:

#Passed: Test's Complete
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish and power OFF.
DISPLAY: AllTestsPassed.png
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
EXE: CloseWinCam.bat
// End of file
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
